When an unmarshalling error occurs in streaming mode after some chunks have already been sent (line 241-244), returning with c.JSON will mix JSON error responses with the newline-delimited streaming format, potentially confusing clients. Consider sending errors in the same streaming format when prompt.Stream is true, or documenting this edge case behavior.
```suggestion
			if prompt.Stream {
				// In streaming mode, send the error in the same streaming format
				_ = writeOllamaResponse(c, prompt.Model, "Error: failed to parse upstream response", false)
			} else {
				c.JSON(http.StatusInternalServerError, gin.H{"error": "testing endpoint"})
			}
			return
		}
		if fabricResponse.Type == "error" {
			if prompt.Stream {
				// In streaming mode, send the upstream error as a streamed chunk
				_ = writeOllamaResponse(c, prompt.Model, fmt.Sprintf("Error: %s", fabricResponse.Content), false)
			} else {
				c.JSON(http.StatusInternalServerError, gin.H{"error": fabricResponse.Content})
			}
```

The HTTP response status code from the upstream Fabric server is not being checked. If the Fabric server returns a non-2xx status code (e.g., 400, 404, 500), the code will still attempt to process the response body as if it were successful. This could lead to parsing errors or incorrect responses being sent to the client. Consider checking fabricRes.StatusCode and handling non-success status codes appropriately before processing the response body.
```suggestion
	defer fabricRes.Body.Close()

	if fabricRes.StatusCode < http.StatusOK || fabricRes.StatusCode >= http.StatusMultipleChoices {
		bodyBytes, readErr := io.ReadAll(fabricRes.Body)
		if readErr != nil {
			log.Printf("Upstream Fabric server returned non-2xx status %d and body could not be read: %v", fabricRes.StatusCode, readErr)
		} else {
			log.Printf("Upstream Fabric server returned non-2xx status %d: %s", fabricRes.StatusCode, string(bodyBytes))
		}

		errorMessage := fmt.Sprintf("upstream Fabric server returned status %d", fabricRes.StatusCode)
		if prompt.Stream {
			_ = writeOllamaResponse(c, prompt.Model, fmt.Sprintf("Error: %s", errorMessage), true)
		} else {
			c.JSON(fabricRes.StatusCode, gin.H{"error": errorMessage})
		}
		return
	}
```

